  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>In the continuation of Marinières beach, the Ange Gardien is a small, somewhat hidden pebble cove with views over the Villefranche bay.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Several unofficial directories present this cove as open to dogs, but the Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office does not include it among the dog-allowed beaches: in Villefranche-sur-Mer it lists only Deux Rups beach ("dogs are allowed on this beach"), and specifies that outside the listed zones dogs are not admitted on the metropolitan area's beaches. We found no municipal order. To be sure not to risk a fine, favour Deux Rups beach and call the town hall before coming.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: for a break with your dog in Villefranche, aim first for Deux Rups beach, the only one the tourist office cites.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The old town of Villefranche, with its picturesque harbour and the Saint-Pierre chapel decorated by Cocteau, is worth a stroll after the swim.</p>
    </div>

